Frequency / Counting Array Pattern

Core Idea

Count what you have → subtract what you need → negative means impossible.

int cnt[26] = {};
for(char c : a) cnt[c - 'a']++;   // available
for(char c : s) cnt[c - 'a']--;   // required
for(int x : cnt)
    if(x < 0) return NO;

Recognition Trigger

Use this when you see:

* Anagrams
* Construct a string
* Available characters
* Character frequency
* “Can we make X from Y?”

Formula

Available − Required ≥ 0 → Possible

Complexity

* Time: O(total characters)
* Space: O(26) → O(1)

Memory Trick

+ Have → − Need → Negative = NO
